    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=0885b537-c9f5-47f8-aa4f-0ad7bbebf412&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9206796490566_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's and Women's Golf Coach",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL Assistant Men's and Women's Golf Coach Staff Full-Time Athletics - Golf 30+ days ago Requisition ID: 1710 Apply Salary: $30,000.00 Annually Randolph-Macon College invites applications for a full-time, 12- month Assistant Men’s and Women’s Golf Coach. Reporting to the Director of Golf, the assistant coach will help plan and execute practices and game plans for a competitive NCAA Division III program. Responsibilities Teach the fundamentals of the sport by providing hands-on instruction, demonstrating proper techniques, and offering feedback to enhance student-athlete performance. Instruct team members individually and in groups, demonstrate game techniques, and assist with position-specific skill development. Devise and implement game strategies, position assignments, practice sessions, and game plans in accordance with NCAA and conference regulations. Take an active role in game-day strategy, instruct student-athletes accordingly, and scout opponents to develop effective game strategies. Instruct athletes on physical health and safety while serving as an academic and personal mentor. Recruit qualified student-athletes through travel, outreach to high school coaches, and communication with prospective student-athletes. Assist with team travel, equipment issue, maintenance, and inventory. Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Coach. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and previous competitive playing experience at the college or university level required; previous coaching experience preferred. Knowledge of the sport, including skills and strategies of the game. Successful applicant must demonstrate strong leadership and interpersonal skills as well as be committed to the policies and regulations of the NCAA Division III. Must be or become certified in CPR and first aid techniques. Must have a valid driver’s license with satisfactory motor vehicle record by insurance standards. The College Founded in 1830, Randolph-Macon has about 1800 students and is located in Ashland, VA, a residential community 15 miles north of Richmond and 90 miles south of Washington D.C., thereby having all the benefits for its students, faculty and staff of a dynamic metropolitan area which serves as the state capital. Over 85% of students reside on campus. For more information about the College see www.rmc.edu . Randolph-Macon College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Application Please complete an online application at https://bit.ly/4fCtQGH to include uploading a resume, letter of interest, and contact information for two professional references addressed to: Claudia Burcham, HR Generalist. Screening of applications will begin immediately. Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
